column119:
You're wrong. The 'property' is a method on the Function prototype - take a closer look.<p>Anyway, style does matter and were this line written with readability in mind you wouldn't make this mistake.<p>Also, I would definitely abstract over @get and property:<p><pre><code>    makeProperty = (attrs...) -> 
        func = () -> (@get(x) for x in attrs).join(" ")
        func.property(attrs...)

    MyApp.president = Ember.Object.create(
        fullName: makeProperty("firstName", "lastName")
    )
</code></pre>
The parens after create are not needed, the next indented line should tell us that this is a function with arguments, but I don't mind them here.
